TITLE='Authentic title "How Two Incomes Made the Middle Class POORER" is a paradox frame. The script delivers it via the Two-Income Trap thesis, but its headline comparison mixes today\'s dollars (1973 family) with early-2000s dollars (two-earner family), so the narrated numbers contradict "75% more" and "$800 less" even though the direction holds.'
THUMB='Registered maxresdefault 1280x720 (HTTP 200, real image). White background: the recurring cartoon man, shocked; "MORE MONEY... POORER?!" in heavy black capitals; an arrow from a large cash pile to a smaller one with scattered coins. At 320x180 the words and both piles read clearly. Matches the paradox thesis.'
SCRIPT='A single-narrator story essay with composites: Hazel/Nico hook, Tom/Susan (1973) vs Justin/Kimberly (early 2000s) from The Two-Income Trap, the not-frivolous-spending rebuttal, housing price-to-income and the mortgage bidding war, school-district premiums, childcare costs and HHS benchmark, second-earner taxes, the lost backup earner and Fisher-Johnson bankruptcy evidence, Nico\'s month, BofA paycheck-to-paycheck data, Hazel\'s net contribution, Ezra/Lily\'s one-income plan, 28/36 of one income and a callback close. Mostly sourced; the family comparison mixes dollar bases and Hazel\'s subtraction chain is wrong.'
